--- what each section covers ---
Everywhere ["app/**/*.rb", "docs/*.md"] -> ["app/billing/charge.rb", "app/order.rb", "docs/overview.md"]
Billing ["app/billing/*.rb"] -> ["app/billing/charge.rb"]
--- one glob two sections share ---
.spec/glossary.md ["7 app/**/*.rb"]
--- effective vocabulary per file ---
app/billing/charge.rb Customer: Whoever the order is fulfilled for.
app/billing/charge.rb Customer rejects User: Nobody logs in to place an order.
app/billing/charge.rb Order: The billable set of lines.
app/billing/charge.rb Order rejects Invoice: An invoice is issued later, from an order.
app/order.rb Customer: Whoever the order is fulfilled for.
app/order.rb Customer rejects User: Nobody logs in to place an order.
app/order.rb Order: What a customer asks us to fulfil.
app/order.rb Order rejects Purchase: Order is what the domain calls it.
docs/overview.md Customer: Whoever the order is fulfilled for.
docs/overview.md Customer rejects User: Nobody logs in to place an order.
docs/overview.md Order: What a customer asks us to fulfil.
docs/overview.md Order rejects Purchase: Order is what the domain calls it.
--- read backwards, the first section lands on top ---
app/billing/charge.rb Order: What a customer asks us to fulfil.
--- what the specification spells is not a use of it ---
app/order.rb:2 Order rejects Purchase: Order is what the domain calls it.
--- a mention the specification set aside, and one it did not ---
app/other.rb:3 Order rejects Purchase: Order is what the domain calls it.
ignored.md:20 nothing at app/gone.rb:9 has Order rejecting Purchase; the line moved or the wording was fixed
--- a missing glossary is a broken reference line, not a difference ---
no glossary at test/fixtures/glossary/absent.md; sumi init lays one down
--- and so is one that never says it is a vocabulary ---
test/fixtures/glossary/titleless.md:1 declares no title; sumi help glossary has the form
--- an ignore that could not be written down is a broken reference line ---
test/fixtures/glossary/noat.md:12 writes an ignore that does not name a line in backticks; sumi help glossary has the form
test/fixtures/glossary/noreason.md:12 writes an ignore at app/order.rb:2 with no reason; sumi help glossary has the form
--- a name the vocabulary spells twice where it stands for one thing ---
test/fixtures/glossary/secondsection.md:16 opens a second section named Everywhere, first opened at test/fixtures/glossary/secondsection.md:6; sumi help glossary has the form
test/fixtures/glossary/secondterm.md:26 declares Order a second time in Billing, first declared at test/fixtures/glossary/secondterm.md:22; sumi help glossary has the form
--- and one named absolutely still answers where the run started ---
no glossary at test/fixtures/glossary/absent.md; sumi init lays one down
